/** @page mptkevent_concept MPTKEvent Concept and Data Model
 *  @brief Understand what MPTKEvent represents and how to use it in playback workflows.
 *
 *  @details
 *  @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent "MPTKEvent" is the central runtime MIDI message object in Maestro MPTK.
 *  It represents one MIDI event (note, controller, patch change, meta event, etc.)
 *  and is used by both file-based and real-time playback systems.
 *
 *  In practice:
 *  - MidiFilePlayer reads and emits lists of MPTKEvent.
 *  - MidiStreamPlayer plays MPTKEvent instances created at runtime.
 *  - MPTKWriter and related APIs generate MIDI content through MPTKEvent-compatible data.
 *
 *  @section mptkevent_model Core Model
 *
 *  The event type is defined by @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Command "Command".
 *  Other fields are interpreted from that command:
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Value "Value": note number, controller value, patch index, tempo/signature packed data, etc.
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Channel "Channel": MIDI channel (0 to 15).
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Velocity "Velocity": mainly for note on/off events.
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Duration "Duration": note length in milliseconds for NoteOn events.
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Controller "Controller": controller type for ControlChange.
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Meta "Meta" and @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.Info "Info": meta-event subtype and text data.
 *
 *  Related enums:
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKCommand
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKController
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKMeta
 *
 *  @section mptkevent_runtime Typical Runtime Usage
 *
 *  A common real-time workflow is:
 *  - create a new MPTKEvent,
 *  - set Command and required message data,
 *  - send it with @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiStreamPlayer.MPTK_PlayEvent "MPTK_PlayEvent()",
 *  - optionally stop a sustained note with @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiStreamPlayer.MPTK_StopEvent "MPTK_StopEvent()".
 *
 *  @code
 *  // Play C4 on channel 0 for 500 ms
 *  MPTKEvent e = new MPTKEvent()
 *  {
 *      Command = MPTKCommand.NoteOn,
 *      Value = 60,
 *      Velocity = 100,
 *      Channel = 0,
 *      Duration = 500
 *  };
 *  midiStreamPlayer.MPTK_PlayEvent(e);
 *  @endcode
 *
 *  @section mptkevent_timing Timing and Context
 *
 *  MPTKEvent also stores timeline and runtime context information:
 *  - musical position: Tick, Measure, Beat,
 *  - real-time position: RealTime,
 *  - session/source context: IdSession, Source,
 *  - attached active voices: Voices, and completion state: IsOver.
 *
 *  These fields are useful for diagnostics, filtering, editor tools, and
 *  synchronization logic around playback.
 *
 *  @section mptkevent_pro Maestro Pro Extension
 *
 *  In Maestro Pro, MPTKEvent adds per-event SoundFont generator controls
 *  (real-time timbre changes):
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.ModifySynthParameter "ModifySynthParameter()",
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent.ClearSynthParameter "ClearSynthParameter()",
 *  - generator query helpers (default/current value, labels, generator list).
 *
 *  @see @ref midistreamplayer_realtime
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MPTKEvent
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiStreamPlayer.MPTK_PlayEvent
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_ReadMidiEvents
 */
